---
source: crates/wolf_mem/tests/mem_diagnostics.rs
expression: render_mem(src)
---
error[E1006]: `S` holds a strong `shared` path back to itself
 --> mem:///main.lu:1:12
  |
1 | struct S { next: shared S }
  |            ^^^^ this `shared` edge closes the cycle S → S
  |
  = note: strong `shared` references drop their target when the last count drops, so a strong
    cycle would keep itself alive forever — and wolf has no cycle collector
    ([mem.shared.rc.2]). Break the back-edge: make this field `weak S` (upgrade to reach the
    value without keeping it alive) or `handle S` (a generational index that faults if the
    target is gone). If the structure is genuinely cyclic, keep the whole graph in one
    region instead — intra-region cycles are safe and freed wholesale
    ([mem.region.intra.1]).
